{
	"name": "Carving a Path",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/skills/melee/shield-damaged-broken-orange.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>At 14th level, you gain the ability to rush through enemy lines, opening the way for your allies. To carve a path you must make a @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-class-features.Item.5j1UqnHUHm5MGDQx]{Spellstrike} on at least on target, and may use @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-class-features.Item.fpDSuAyOdOmXu7zU]{Multistrike} to hit a maximum of three targets. You must move at least five feet between each target struck, and can only attack each target once. A creature struck by this ability must make a Strength save against your spellcasting DC or lose their reaction.</p><p>If they succeed at the saving throw, they must use their reaction to attack you if you leave their threatened area.</p>",
